        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Nike, Inc., Wieden+Kennedy\n- Products: Just Do It, Swoosh\n- People: Dan Wieden\n- Places: Portland, Oregon\n- Topics: trademarks, logos, advertising\n\nFacts:\n- Dan Wieden, born in 1945, is an American advertising executive who co-founded Wieden+Kennedy.\n- Dan Wieden coined Nike's tagline \"Just Do It.\"\n- \"Just Do It\" is a trademark of Nike and a core component of Nike's brand.\n- The Swoosh is the logo of American athletic shoe and clothing manufacturer Nike, Inc.\n- The Swoosh has become one of the most recognizable brand logos in the world.\n- The Swoosh alone has been valued at $26 billion.\n- The 60-second advertisement \"Pretty\" was handled by Wieden+Kennedy in Portland, Oregon.",
